---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GradientText from "../../components/GradientText.astro";
import PlayableNav from "../../components/PlayableNav.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playable Ads Development | Aniloom Technologies" description="HTML5/WebGL playable ad development with responsive layouts, release-quality review, and production handoff. Custom art and additional variants are scoped separately.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <PlayableNav />
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--service section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Playable Ads / Development</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>Playable ad development, from concept to <GradientText>delivery.</GradientText></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead" data-reveal>We build HTML5/WebGL playable ads from an approved concept or reference. The base package includes portrait and landscape layouts, QA, and production files with source handoff.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions" data-reveal><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss development</button><a class="text-link" href="#scope">See the scope <span>↓</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="service-intro section-shell section-pad" id="scope">
      <div class="service-intro__statement" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">One connected delivery</p><h2>A playable built to your brief and target specification.</h2><p>Before production, we agree on the interaction, supplied assets, target provider, review rounds, and delivery requirements. Custom art and additional variants are priced separately.</p></div>
      <div class="service-scope-grid">
        <article data-reveal><span>01</span><h3>Shape the experience</h3><p>Clarify the campaign role, core interaction, user journey, call to action, end card, acceptance criteria, and known constraints.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>02</span><h3>Build the interaction</h3><p>Implement the experience in HTML5/WebGL, including UI, visual assets, animation, responsive rules, and the agreed integration behavior.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>03</span><h3>Review and prepare</h3><p>Check the journey and responsive states, record corrections, retest changes, prepare variants, and make remaining release risk visible.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system-band section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Development-integrated quality</p><h2>Testing starts during development.</h2></div><p>Engineering implements the playable. Quality Engineering checks the interaction and layouts, records issues, and retests corrections against the agreed acceptance criteria.</p></div>
        <div class="role-grid">
          <article data-reveal><span>Engineering</span><h3>Implementation and technical decisions</h3><p>Architecture, runtime behavior, rendering, interactions, responsive implementation, integrations, and technical corrections remain engineering responsibilities.</p></article>
          <article data-reveal><span>Quality Engineering</span><h3>Interaction testing and visual review</h3><p>QA checks instructions, controls, text, layout, and feedback in portrait and landscape, then documents findings and retest results.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deliverable section-shell section-pad">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Possible scope</p><h2>Base package and optional production work.</h2></div><p>The base package uses your approved assets and includes one language, one behavioral variant, and one provider package. See pricing for the full scope and add-ons.</p></div>
      <div class="deliverable-grid">
        <div data-reveal><span>Concept and flow</span><p>An approved concept or reference, one core interaction, and agreed acceptance criteria.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Implementation</span><p>HTML5/WebGL engineering, UI behavior, responsive layout, animation, and technical integration.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Creative production</span><p>Implementation uses client-supplied approved assets. Custom UI, 2D or 3D art, and substantial animation are separate production add-ons.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Release preparation</span><p>The agreed provider package, click-through or analytics hooks, review findings, production files, and source handoff. Extra variants and localization are add-ons.</p></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="scope-note" data-reveal><strong>Development package</strong><p>Starting at $5,000 USD. The planning range is 10-15 business days after complete inputs and access. The proposal confirms the final scope and timeline. <a href="/playable-ads/pricing/">See the package and add-ons</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

    <section class="service-crosslink section-shell" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Inspect working examples</p><div><h2>Try our playable demonstrations.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/case-studies/magic-thai-playables/">Explore the Magic Thai demonstrations <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="service-crosslink section-shell" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Already have a build?</p><div><h2>Start with QA and release readiness instead.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/qa-release-readiness/">Explore the review path <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="callout section-shell section-pad" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Start with the campaign goal</p><h2>Tell us about your playable ad.</h2><p>Share the approved concept or reference, assets, target provider specification, and deadline. We will confirm the scope and delivery plan.</p><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss development</button></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
